    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d704">

                <pb facs="0655" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10895a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="77"
                        xml:id="d704-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-29T13:00:00-05:00">October 29, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. According to an Associated Press report from Shanghai of October 29 the
                    German Ambassador was stated to be in Nanking acting as a mediator and messenger
                    carrying proposed Japanese peace terms.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d704-f2"/> The
                    report states further that the German Ambassador recently spent a week in
                    Shanghai in conference with the Japanese Ambassador and other high
                    officials.</p>
                <p>The Department has received information to this same general effect attributed to
                        Suma.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d704-f3"/></p>
                <p>Please telegraph urgently what you can discreetly ascertain in regard to this
                    report and your estimate as to its significance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d704-f1" n="77" type="source" xml:id="d704-f1-content">
                <p>The same as No. 273 to the Ambassador In Japan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d704-f2" n="78" xml:id="d704-f2-content">
                <p>See Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Documents on German Foreign
                        Policy, 1918–1945</hi>, series D, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                    pp. 733 ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d704-f3" n="79" xml:id="d704-f3-content">
                <p>Japanese Counselor of Embassy in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
